{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"I’d assess **economic viability, not AUM alone**:\n\n- **Break-even AUM:** Estimate annual revenue (AUM × fee rate, plus any other sponsor revenue) against fixed and variable costs: administration, custody, audit, legal, index licensing, marketing, and distribution. A low fee or costly strategy may need substantial scale.\n- **Who bears the shortfall:** Check fee waivers, expense caps, subsidy commitments, their end dates, and whether the sponsor can absorb losses. A fund can operate below break-even if support is credible and ongoing.\n- **Seed quality and persistence:** Identify whether seed assets come from the sponsor, affiliates, employees, or independent investors; assess concentration, lockups, redemption terms, and incentives to remain. A large but temporary or affiliated seed may overstate durable demand.\n- **Flows and liquidity:** Track net flows, holder concentration, bid–ask spreads, trading volume, and market-maker support. Persistent outflows or fragile liquidity can raise costs and weaken the case to continue.\n- **Sponsor capacity and behavior:** Consider the firm’s resources, product-launch record, stated scale thresholds, and willingness to consolidate or close funds.\n\nThese are warning signs, not a closure forecast."}}
